  m_Name: Blade15
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade15
  description: The Blade15 is a tiny, elongated blade situated at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, constructed from Blades texture material, responsible for
    channeling and accelerating the air through the engine, with a notable feature
    being its textured surface that reduces turbulence and enhances airflow, allowing
    for more efficient energy transfer. Its elongated shape provides a larger surface
    area, and its position in the compressor stage makes it crucial for the engine's
    ability to produce high thrust levels. By optimizing airflow and minimizing losses,
    Blade15 plays a vital role in the engine's overall efficiency and performance,
    making it an essential component of the jet engine's compressor stage.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
